BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:012a441fc33f3832a3691279@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260829T180420Z
SUMMARY:LITTLE WOMEN (2019)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Browning Cinema Professor Pfinklepfunder's $1 Sunday Films Dire
 cted by Greta Gerwig With Saoirse Ronan\, Emma Watson\, Florence Pugh Rat
 ed PG\, 135 minutes\, Blu-ray The four March sisters have been part of Am
 erican libraries and reading nooks for almost as long as the University o
 f Notre Dame has been around. Louisa May Alcott's timeless band of sister
 s has been adapted for film previously\, but perhaps never with as much p
 anache or splash as when Greta Gerwig (director of Barbie) released this 
 film as the pandemic was dawning. Meg (Emma Watson) \, Jo (Saoirse Ronan)
  \, Beth (Eliza Scanlen) \, and Amy (Florence Pugh) experience the many s
 easons of New England life\, including the rivalries\, heartbreaks\, and 
 joys that come with such a warm home. Sponsored by the Meg and John P. Br
 ogan Endowment for Classic Cinema.\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbe
 nd.com/events/little-women-2019/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/little-women-2019/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260830T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260830T143000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
